.TH TLLAMAD 1 "November 2026" "TLlama" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tllamad \- foreground TLlama inference daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tllamad
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tllamad
.RI [ options ] " repo check|prune|inspect|stats " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tllamad
serves model APIs and supervises private native tllama-server workers.
It stays in the foreground. The Debian package supplies tllamad.service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --list-devices
Forward the selected native runtime's device table and exit without starting
the server or loading a model. Cannot be combined with configuration inspection
or repository commands. Normal configuration/runtime-path selection still applies.
.TP
.B --config FILE
Select a server TOML configuration file explicitly.
.TP
.B --no-config
Skip configuration-file discovery.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate the effective configuration and exit without starting a server.
.TP
.B --print-config
Print effective configuration values and their sources, then exit.
.TP
.B --host ADDRESS
Listener address. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B --port PORT
Listener port. Default: 54800.
.TP
.B --models-dir DIRECTORY
Model repository root. Default: /var/lib/tllama/models.
.TP
.B --runtime-path FILE
Absolute path to the private native runtime executable.
.TP
.B --device DEVICE
Global default native device selection.
.TP
.B --backend-priority LIST
Comma-separated backend priority.
.TP
.B --help
Show all options and corresponding environment variables.
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed daemon version.
.SH LOCAL REPOSITORY COMMANDS
These one-shot commands run on the repository filesystem as its intended
service account. They do not start/contact HTTP or load native workers.
Normal storage configuration applies; --models-dir is an optional override.
--config, --no-config and --models-dir work before repo or after the operation.
.TP
.B repo check [--hashes] [--json]
Read-only integrity check. --hashes independently verifies weight content
addresses. Missing/legacy stores are reported, not initialized or repaired.
.TP
.B repo prune [--apply] [--json]
Preview complete unreferenced and unreserved groups and their owned
cache/upload aliases. --apply performs fresh checks under the repository lock
through deletion. Interrupted work remains in the durable cleanup retry queue.
Independent caches and staging/download leftovers are not swept.
.TP
.B repo inspect MODEL [--json]
Explain all component groups, shards, sharing and protection for a definition.
.TP
.B repo inspect --group SHA256 [--json]
Inspect a data group by its lowercase SHA-256 identifier instead of a model.
.TP
.B repo stats [--json]
Read-only group/sharing counts and managed weight byte accounting.
Candidate weight bytes are not guaranteed freed disk space.
.PP
Exit status is 0 for success, 1 for findings/incomplete inspection or deletion
errors, 2 for CLI/configuration errors and 130 for Ctrl+C.
All daemons sharing a repository must use the current reservation protocol
before physical reclamation. Old/external readers cannot be detected.
Existing unmarked repositories require offline conversion with writers stopped;
the converter is in the optional tllama-doc package.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Global precedence is command line, environment, server TOML, built-in defaults.
File selection is --config, TLLAMA_CONFIG, the user's tllama/server.toml under
XDG_CONFIG_HOME (or ~/.config), then /etc/tllama/server.toml.
The first existing default file is used, without merging files.
Relative paths use the daemon's working directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tllama/server.toml
System service configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/tllama/models
Default model repository.
.TP
.I /var/cache/tllama/huggingface
Hugging Face cache used by the packaged service.
.TP
.I /run/tllama
Private worker runtime directory used by the packaged service.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/tllama/server/tllama-server
Native runtime supplied by the separate tllama-server package.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tllama (1),
